<p>Colombia has authorized euthanasia to curb the growing population of hippos descended from four animals that drug trafficker Pablo Escobar illegally imported in 1981, after officials said no other country agreed to take them and earlier control efforts proved costly or ineffective. Environment Minister Irene Vélez said the measure could affect up to 80 hippos, though authorities have not said when the killings will begin. The animals have become both a tourist curiosity and a growing environmental and public-safety problem in central Colombia, where authorities say they are displacing native species and threatening nearby residents. Officials warned that without stronger population controls, the herd could grow to as many as 1,000 by 2035, underscoring why Colombia is now turning to a tougher option after trying sterilization and relocation.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/9aFXdomWDMx3f_lAwebIUgTLKINMY-RSgvI5UVrfaPumKmjpxWZGF6GViV74MmDmWU-jgoZSIxmFOnL8IPv-SeGsL2-jFlClqpgPW3mcZvrlTbGjOsmQu8kl5fmsGSaPwXj2_63NbptlVBt0abzEC6tNx8woA56gn44BovpcD4uyIpQT_iM2FQR5ATO1viDwWAs1FV6dGX3BGSAJB23zNInYeSuuLWAzN2-GugE' alt='Hippos in Colombia, in February 2021.' /><br /><blockquote>The administrative silence tells us there is no interest in receiving them - Irene Vélez</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Colombian environment ministry: The ministry&#x27;s case centers on the collapse of relocation abroad, with Irene Vélez saying the lack of response from other countries showed that option had effectively run out of road. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-04-13/colombia-authorizes-the-use-of-euthanasia-to-stop-the-spread-of-pablo-escobars-hippos.html'>El País</a>)</li><li>Conservation and safety angle: Officials said the intervention serves two goals at once — limiting harm to native species while reducing risks for villagers living near the hippos&#x27; range. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/13/colombia-hippo-hunt-pablo-escobar'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Public-debate angle: The hippos&#x27; popularity with visitors has made the issue more politically and culturally complicated than a typical invasive-species case. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/13/colombia-to-cull-hippo-population-founded-by-drug-lord'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-04-13/colombia-authorizes-the-use-of-euthanasia-to-stop-the-spread-of-pablo-escobars-hippos.html'>Colombia authorizes the use of euthanasia to stop the spread of Pablo Escobar’s hippos</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/13/colombia-hippo-hunt-pablo-escobar'>Colombia to cull up to 80 hippos descended from Pablo Escobar zoo</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/13/colombia-to-cull-hippo-population-founded-by-drug-lord'>Colombia to cull up to 80 hippos linked to drug lord Pablo Escobar</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/colombia-to-euthanize-cocaine-hippos-pablo-escobar/'>Colombia to kill dozens of &quot;cocaine hippos&quot; linked to Pablo Escobar</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/colombia-to-control-hippo-population-through-euthanasia'>Colombia to control hippo population linked to drug lord Pablo Escobar through euthanasia</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>